d5=A.bh(d2,"9-1",A.a([d1,c9,c3,d4,A.h(f7,0,A.a([0,1],p),"A bluff only changes what opponents believe is safe, which creates claim chances but guarantees no win and scores nothing by itself.",d5,f7,"What does a successful decoy discard actually buy you? (Select all that apply)",f7,B.D),A.h(f7,0,f7,"Each pattern is read from the information the player releases, so an unusually clean story is itself a warning sign.",B.p,B.So,"Match each discard pattern to the deception or intent it suggests.",f7,B.G),A.h(A.a(["not","never"],k7),0,f7,"Players shed what they are certain is useless first, so a turn-one discard is read as real information about their hand.",B.p,f7,"Early discards are the strongest signal because players throw the tiles they are sure they will ___ need.",f7,B.A),A.h(f7,1,f7,"Experienced players treat a suspiciously clean discard pattern as possible deception rather than proof.",A.a(["Trust the pattern completely","Question the pattern, because it may be a counter-bluff","Ignore all of their discards","Assume they have no plan at all"],k7),f7,"An opponent's discards look almost too perfect for the flush they seem to be abandoning. What does the lesson advise?",f7,B.i)],o),j7,"Misleading opponents through discards","Bluffing & Deception")
